-- cmd: check
-- exit: 1
-- stderr-contains: unknown method 'tagged' on type Int
-- A module calls the methods of the traits whose modules it imports
-- (or they import, and so on). `c` does not import `a`: whether `a`
-- was checked before `c` or after it, `c` has no method `tagged`.
-- (It once had it when an earlier import had brought the impl in. The
-- help that names the module is there only when `a` is checked first.)
import c
import a

fn main() {
  println(c.v())
  println(a.touch())
}
